    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1070">

                <pb facs="1328" n="1314" sameAs="frus:frus1945v09/pg1314"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 E W /1–3045: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Peru</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">White</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Extract]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lima</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-01-30T11:00:00-05:00">January 30,
                            1945—11 a.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 1:30 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>96. I yesterday handed Foreign Minister enclosure secret despatch 3840 January 26
                    for delivery addressee, apprised him of content, requesting information as to
                    progress.</p>
                <pb facs="1329" n="1315" xml:id="pg1315"/>
                <p>He said that for internal political reasons he was exploring possibility avoiding
                    special session Congress, thus reversing his stand reported telegram 54, January
                    16, 1 p.m.<anchor n="11" xml:id="d1070-f1"/>
                </p>
                <p rendition="#center">. . . . . . . . . . . . . .</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">White</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d1070-f1" n="11" xml:id="d1070-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed; the Foreign Minister was reported as foreseeing no obstacles, “not
                    excluding summoning of special session of Congress.” (740.0011 EW/1–1745)</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
